int json_frame_write_fmt(int fd, int channel, const char *fmt, ...);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convenience wrapper around \f[CR]json_frame_write(3)\f[R] that formats
the payload using \f[CR]printf\f[R]\-style format specifiers.
The formatted string is passed as the frame payload with
\f[CR]flags\f[R] set to 0.
.PP
The function first attempts formatting into a stack\-allocated buffer of
\f[CR]SERVER_MAX_LINE\f[R] (8192) bytes.
If the formatted output exceeds this size, a heap buffer is dynamically
allocated.
.PP
This is the primary function used throughout the v2 session handler for
sending JSON responses.
